Chapter: TypeNameExistence

 The controls for CDX3008. Every shape here reaches the same ANamedType arm
 that refuses a phantom type, and every one of them is legal, so a check
 that refuses any of these is wrong in the expensive direction. Holder names
 Later BEFORE Later is defined, which is the case that made a refusal
 inside resolution impossible: the type-def map is built incrementally and a
 record's fields resolve against the partial map.

 We say:

Section: Types

  Holder = record { item : Later, vec : Vector 4 Integer }

  Later = record { n : Integer }

Section: Body

  count-of : List a -> Integer
  count-of (xs) = list-length xs

  n-of : Later -> Integer
  n-of (l) = l.n

  vec-arity : Vector 4 Integer -> Integer
  vec-arity (v) = 4

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("tvar " & show (count-of [1, 2, 3]))
    print-line-uni ("forward " & show (n-of (Later { n = 9 })))
  end